1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,400
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:22,980
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:29,980
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:52,980 --> 00:01:12,560
Why you can't imagine being lost until a single minute.

5
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:42,180
It's fun!

6
00:01:42,560 --> 00:02:09,500
The day begins early for a magic night, there is much to be done before the sun goes down.

7
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:40,560
There is cleaning, laundry, my heart belongs to Sister Lily and I won't betray her for anybody!

8
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,560
Ahhhh!

9
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,560
Next!

10
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,560
Tending to the Beasts

11
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:54,560
Sit, Beastie!

12
00:02:55,560 --> 00:03:00,560
Yeah, good boy! I think you've earned a treat. Go on.

13
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:07,560
Feeding them even if it turns out you're on the menu for breakfast. And then...

14
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:16,560
Hey, Captain Yami! Captain!

15
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:22,560
The unbelievable task of waking up Yami Sukihiro, Captain of the Black Bulls.

16
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:25,560
Captain, sir! It's morning!

17
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:28,560
Shut up now or I will kill you!

18
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:30,560
Yes, sir! Sorry, sir!

19
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:34,560
You're the one who told me to wake you up every morning!

20
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:40,560
It is also a magic night's duty to put up with the whims of their sometimes fickle captain.

21
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:52,560
Another day of backbreaking manual labor. Being in a magic night squad is a lot more work than I expected.

22
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:59,560
How is this any different from what I did back at the church? What does a magic night squad do?

23
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:07,560
First thing in the morning, meat, meat, and more meat.

24
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:13,560
Hey, Noelle! How come you don't ever help out with the cleaning and stuff?

25
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,560
The cleaning? I'm royalty, you know.

26
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,560
And a new recruit!

27
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:21,560
I've never done any cleaning or laundry in my life. Why would I start now?

28
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:28,560
Are you bragging about being lazy? Come on, we're on the same squad here! Ever heard the term team effort?

29
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:29,560
I am royalty!

30
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,560
Yeah, and you won't let us forget it!

31
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,560
Silence, insect!

32
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,560
We're back to that?

33
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:38,560
Hey, uh, just wondering, what exactly does a magic night squad do?

34
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,560
Huh?

35
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:44,560
Are you seriously serious right now?

36
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:49,560
We protect the country, you idiot! Keep the people safe! It's the manliest job in the world!

37
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:53,560
Why'd you even want to join up if you were so freakin' clueless, huh?

38
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,560
Well, answer me!

39
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,560
I'm sorry, I just wanted to be done with the video!

40
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,560
Why did you even take the exam if you don't know what we do?

41
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:03,560
Well, those two are certainly chipper, aren't they?

42
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,560
Anybody? Anybody?

43
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,560
Anybody?

44
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,560
No?

45
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:07,560
This one!

46
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:08,560
This is the kind of idiot!

47
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,560
This is the kind of idiot!

48
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,560
You stupid dick coming to our turf without a clue!

49
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:11,560
I don't know how to do!

50
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,560
I don't know how to do!

51
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,560
I don't know how to do!

52
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,560
I don't know how to do!

53
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,560
I don't know how to do that!

54
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,560
Geez!

55
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:19,560
Will someone tell him what a magic night squad does?

56
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:21,560
How about you, wino?

57
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:25,560
Well, uh, we like safeguard the citizens' safety!

58
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:27,560
You know, that sort of thing.

59
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:34,560
And as a bonus, you can get to know some marvelous gentlemen while you're on guard duty.

60
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:35,560
Oh, okay!

61
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:36,560
Hmm.

62
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:39,560
Well, if you ask me, the best part's all the people you get to fight!

63
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:43,560
You can spend hours beating up a criminal and nobody will even think twice about it!

64
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:46,560
More than anything, it's an excellent career.

65
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,560
One that makes my sister proud.

66
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,560
See her?

67
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,560
Marie?

68
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:53,560
I use my wages to buy her nice things.

69
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:56,560
Remember, if you lay a finger on her, then you die!

70
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:00,560
Okay, and what about you?

71
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:04,560
Saving women left and right, making all of them want you.

72
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,560
What more could you ask for?

73
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:12,560
I can tell you right anymore, you're scared because we're friends.

74
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,560
What's wrong, Charmy?

75
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,560
How did this happen?

76
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:19,560
This is awful!

77
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,560
The food is off!

78
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,560
It's all gone!

79
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:26,560
I'm nowhere near full!

80
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,560
Cotton creation magic!

81
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:31,560
Bring on the sheep hooks!

82
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,560
All right!

83
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:42,560
That's more like it!

84
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:49,560
The most important thing is when you're in a magic night squad, you can eat like crazy!

85
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,560
Ah!

86
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,560
Munch, munch!

87
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:57,560
Gray?

88
00:06:57,560 --> 00:07:06,560
Well, it's just a good job, you know?

89
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,560
A clone?

90
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:10,560
I'm really looking forward to our first mission together.

91
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,560
Uh, yeah.

92
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:20,560
Man, there are some serious weirdos in this place.

93
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,560
What am I doing?

94
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,560
They're insane!

95
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:25,560
Should I even be in this squad?

96
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,560
Watch closely.

97
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:30,560
You take this, and you do this, and now it's yummy!

98
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,560
So very yummy!

99
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:35,560
Here, you take a bite!

100
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,560
Go on!

101
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,560
I can't!

102
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,560
I'm way too full!

103
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,560
Really!

104
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,560
Well, runt!

105
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:44,560
Are you starting to understand what being a magic knight is all about?

106
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:45,560
Oh, come on!

107
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,560
Just mistake you!

108
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,560
No!

109
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:48,560
Not even a little bit!

110
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,560
I'm coming for a moment.

111
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:50,560
It's not true!

112
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,560
Okay.

113
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,560
You Schwab.

114
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:55,560
Maher.

115
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:59,560
Magna, we're going!

116
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:00,560
Yes, yummy, sir.

117
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,560
What's going on?

118
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:06,560
There's a mission.

119
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,560
A real Magic Knight squad mission.

120
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,560
Hold on!

121
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,560
I'll come to!

122
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:12,440
No way.

123
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:15,300
Can't bring a kid along.

124
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:17,760
This is an important mission.

125
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,760
Only grown-up men allowed.

126
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:23,740
Okay, we'll be back.

127
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:24,640
Bye.

128
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:26,380
Listen, gang.

129
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,660
No breaking stuff while we're gone.

130
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:29,340
Okay.

131
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:31,380
Have fun. Bye.

132
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,140
Captain, will you fight me when you get back, pretty please?

133
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:37,000
Don't be having too long, Captain.

134
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,500
I'll be waiting for you.

135
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:39,560
Hurry back.

136
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:41,280
You don't want to go together, do you?

137
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:45,680
I don't know how much longer I can wait to see Marie.

138
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:48,680
I'm going through withdrawal.

139
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:52,040
I'd like to hit on...

140
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:55,180
I mean, get on a mission, too.

141
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,660
Really? What am I doing here?

142
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:05,940
Captain Yami's going, and he's taking Magna.

143
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,000
They both looked so serious.

144
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:10,140
What kind of mission is this?

145
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:29,020
Oh, man.

146
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,720
This is bad, all right.

147
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:35,060
Totally, seriously, crazy bad.

148
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:42,640
From the looks of it, the two of you are done for.

149
00:09:42,640 --> 00:10:03,700
From the looks of it, the two of you are done for.

150
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:04,700
Flush!

151
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:08,280
Two pair.

152
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:08,860
Nothing.

153
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:13,860
She got us, sir.

154
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:22,360
That'll never get old.

155
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,860
I lost it all.

156
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:26,020
That was over half a year's wages.

157
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,780
It's a pleasure, Magna.

158
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:28,420
Always.

159
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:29,980
You too, Captain.

160
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:35,560
I'll be able to buy a lot of nice souvenirs for the village.

161
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,080
Deal us in for one more hand.

162
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:40,700
Really, sir?

163
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:42,040
Hey, now.

164
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,700
You have nothing left to wager.

165
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,000
Not even underwear.

166
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,160
It's true.

167
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,720
He took everything we had.

168
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:49,760
No, not yet.

169
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:51,580
Here's my offer.

170
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:53,300
One last hand.

171
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,060
That's all.

172
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,440
If we win, then you give us back everything.

173
00:10:56,700 --> 00:10:57,040
Oh.

174
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:58,320
All right.

175
00:10:58,660 --> 00:11:00,020
And what if you lose?

176
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:07,020
Your prize.

177
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:08,420
You're kidding, right, sir?

178
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:10,000
Well, Gramps, what do you say?

179
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:11,060
Please.

180
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:13,120
You can't bet that and you know it.

181
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:13,780
He's right.

182
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:14,680
Come on, Captain.

183
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:15,500
Shut it!

184
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:18,160
This is where we push our limits.

185
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:20,480
I'm not so sure about this.

186
00:11:22,660 --> 00:11:24,000
Hey, here's an idea.

187
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:27,740
You lose to me, and you have to do any one thing I say.

188
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:28,460
Well?

189
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:29,560
Anything.

190
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:30,920
What?

191
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:31,680
Are you crazy?

192
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:33,760
Yami would never agree to that kind of-

193
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:34,440
Kind works.

194
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,240
Yami agrees to the terms of the wager!

195
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:39,740
Come on, Sehi, let's do this!

196
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,420
Say your prayers.

197
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:42,060
Ha!

198
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:44,500
I don't think I'm the one here who needs to be praying.

199
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:13,480
Yeah.

200
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:13,500
Yeah.

201
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:14,680
These'll do.

202
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:27,240
I don't think I'm the one here who's a good beastie.

203
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:33,200
Let's see him.

204
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,460
Okay.

205
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:37,880
There, there.

206
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:39,300
Who's a good beastie?

207
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:40,340
Meat treat?

208
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:49,940
Don't you stand there, help me!

209
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,760
Do I look like I feed animals?

210
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:54,120
You're lucky I even came down here.

211
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:55,400
You should be thanking me.

212
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,360
That's not gonna happen!

213
00:12:56,360 --> 00:13:02,080
I thought I was dead for sure.

214
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,880
You truly are very strong.

215
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:05,340
That's because I train hard!

216
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:08,180
That hand!

217
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:08,860
Captain Yami!

218
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:09,600
I didn't see it coming!

219
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,040
Magna!

220
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:12,960
So then, the mission must be-

221
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:22,140
That old man, he actually pulled out a royal flush.

222
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:24,560
Incredible!

223
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:27,180
Should have known.

224
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:30,360
We didn't stand a chance against old Sehi.

225
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:34,280
He was motivated to beat us today, that's for damn sure.

226
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:38,260
Hey there, Rasta!

227
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:39,600
No, no.

228
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:40,500
We're back!

229
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:43,140
Guess what?

230
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:45,360
I got some news I think you're gonna like.

231
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,780
It's time for your first mission.

232
00:13:47,780 --> 00:13:57,640
Like I said, we've decided to put you in the field.

233
00:13:57,820 --> 00:13:59,140
Alright, our first mission.

234
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:00,160
Here we go.

235
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:01,720
So, what are we doing?

236
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:05,240
I assume it's something befitting royalties such as myself?

237
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:06,200
Yeah!

238
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:07,600
It's a real honor.

239
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:10,600
Go to Saucy Village for some boar hunting.

240
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:11,140
Huh?

241
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:12,600
Hunting boar?

242
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:14,780
Boink!

243
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:19,000
Well, that is a terrible mission.

244
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,720
No, it's not!

245
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:21,960
You take that back!

246
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:24,080
I can break down a boar with my bare hands!

247
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:24,440
Easy!

248
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,060
No, you can't!

249
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,640
Don't even think about trying!

250
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:29,860
Those things are pure evil!

251
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:33,060
They got beady eyes, huge tusks, and they charge for no reason!

252
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:38,400
We lost to the chief of Saucy Village.

253
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:40,280
Now we gotta pay the price.

254
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:40,820
Huh?

255
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:43,540
The two of you lost in a fight?

256
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:44,860
That doesn't even seem possible!

257
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:46,600
How powerful was this man?

258
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:48,400
We lost at poker.

259
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:49,420
At poker?

260
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,620
He literally stripped us of everything we had.

261
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:54,480
Including half a year's wages.

262
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:56,080
Really?

263
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:58,860
Why would you brag about that?

264
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:00,200
That's not all.

265
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:03,540
We also promised we'd do any one thing he requested of us.

266
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:06,300
And that turned out to be getting rid of some boar.

267
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:09,040
There's been a herd of them hanging around near the village.

268
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,280
Trampling fields and causing trouble.

269
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:16,900
Well, I'll head back and wait for you there.

270
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:23,840
Oh, here, you can have these back at least.

271
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:35,520
Can you explain what this has to do with us?

272
00:15:35,660 --> 00:15:36,600
Yes, exactly.

273
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:38,040
You were the ones who lost.

274
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:39,180
It was none of our doing.

275
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,020
So why-

276
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:40,880
You idiots!

277
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:44,420
Do you seriously expect Yami to clean up his own mess?

278
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:46,120
Oh, yeah.

279
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:48,000
It seems reasonable.

280
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,020
Yami doesn't deal with these things.

281
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:51,960
That's what he's got us for.

282
00:15:51,960 --> 00:16:03,280
Either go or die.

283
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:04,760
Your choice.

284
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:05,560
We'll go!

285
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:10,280
So what if it's boar hunting?

286
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:12,060
We're finally going on a mission!

287
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,760
I'm getting pumped now!

288
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:14,380
Yeah!

289
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:19,040
I still don't see why you would be sending me-

290
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,300
Come on!

291
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,000
Do you ever do anything but complain?

292
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:24,700
Actually, that wasn't intended as a complaint.

293
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:26,300
It's just...

294
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:29,380
Given that I can't control my magic power,

295
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:32,280
should I really be going on a mission at all-

296
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:32,740
Dummy!

297
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:35,280
That's the whole point!

298
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:38,020
How do you expect to get any better if you aren't even willing to try?

299
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:43,240
And besides, we're not sending some wet-behind-the-ears recruits out there alone.

300
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:45,460
I'll be around to keep an eye on you two.

301
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,080
Whoa!

302
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,640
You're such a madly man, Magna!

303
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:50,560
Ah, enough of that, Rasta.

304
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:51,400
I'm blushing.

305
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:56,160
Well, if you insist, I suppose I would be willing to accompany you.

306
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:56,940
Really?

307
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:57,980
Wow, thank you.

308
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:58,820
Hey, wait a minute!

309
00:16:58,900 --> 00:17:00,860
How come you're always looking down on us, huh?

310
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:03,380
It isn't that I choose to look down on you.

311
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:06,500
You just always happen to be below me, so what else can I do?

312
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,460
What kind of logic is that?

313
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:12,780
Do your thing!

314
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,660
Use your spatial magic to send us to Saucy Village.

315
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:17,320
Saucy Village?

316
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:20,520
No can do.

317
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:22,920
Come on, it's not like I'm asking a lot-

318
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:23,800
Now, now.

319
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,540
I can go to distant places,

320
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:28,380
but only if I've marked them with my magic power before.

321
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:29,220
Huh?

322
00:17:29,220 --> 00:17:30,640
In other words,

323
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:32,860
you want to go somewhere I've never been?

324
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,000
Sorry, can't do it.

325
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,060
Well, that was a waste of time.

326
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:45,580
Fine, I'll have to go by broom, then.

327
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:48,100
Um, Magnus, sir!

328
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:49,860
Yeah, what is it?

329
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:51,860
I can't fly on a broom!

330
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:53,020
Um...

331
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,160
Yeah, what is it?

332
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,440
What he said.

333
00:17:55,440 --> 00:18:00,280
Are you two kidding me?!

334
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:04,420
You're so completely incompetent that you can't manage something that freaking simple!

335
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:07,440
Oh, you're pretty much the most basic skill of me has!

336
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:09,460
I don't have any magic power, remember?

337
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:12,480
Why do you look so proud?

338
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:15,140
And since I can't control my magic power,

339
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,680
a broom is out of the question.

340
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:17,580
Obviously.

341
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:19,580
And why are you being so arrogant?

342
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:22,220
Fine!

343
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:26,860
We'll just have to ride together.

344
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:29,280
Are you ready to meet my baby?

345
00:18:30,140 --> 00:18:31,040
Your baby?

346
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:34,060
Here it is!

347
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,360
Introducing Crazy Cyclone!

348
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:46,840
I know, right?

349
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:47,940
Awesome, isn't it?

350
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:48,220
Yeah!

351
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:49,080
Way awesome!

352
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:49,900
Try lame.

353
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:50,900
Excuse me?

354
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:54,460
Are you so blind that you can't even recognize beauty when you're staring right at it?

355
00:18:58,200 --> 00:18:59,160
It's lame!

356
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:00,040
Oh...

357
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:00,640
Oh...

358
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:11,820
You can't do it, can you?

359
00:19:12,060 --> 00:19:16,160
A man never goes back on his word!

360
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:18,300
Let's do this thing!

361
00:19:19,380 --> 00:19:21,300
FRIVE!

362
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:24,100
Woo-hoo!

363
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:35,100
There, you see?

364
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:38,180
Crazy Cyclone does just fine, even with three riders!

365
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:40,960
Careful!

366
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:43,440
Are you certain you've flown this thing before?

367
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:45,000
Whoa, newbie!

368
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:46,540
Try not to get so clingy!

369
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:48,020
Silence, you mohawk punk!

370
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:50,240
Now's not the time for name-calling!

371
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:52,800
Oh, yeah!

372
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:55,440
This is amazing, Magna!

373
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,000
We're one with the wind!

374
00:19:57,080 --> 00:19:57,480
Rasta!

375
00:19:57,840 --> 00:19:59,300
You trying to die or something?

376
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:00,500
Hold on!

377
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:00,980
Right!

378
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:05,320
Hey, watch where you put your hands, insect!

379
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:06,980
What the hell are you doing?

380
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:07,600
Back there!

381
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:08,600
RAAAARRRGH!

382
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:37,840
Right on time!

383
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:38,720
Huh?

384
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:55,840
Oh, no!

385
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:56,700
Shh!

386
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:58,440
Oh, yeah!

387
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,560
Oh, my God!

388
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:00,280
Oh, no!

389
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:20,100
So it's here, is it?

390
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,160
The magic stone?

391
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:24,020
Find it.

392
00:21:24,260 --> 00:21:24,620
Sir!

393
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:37,820
In the mist, be lost.

394
00:21:37,820 --> 00:22:07,800
The magic stone?

395
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:14,020
I'll stop on.

396
00:22:15,080 --> 00:22:20,820
We think that the strength is so crazy.

397
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:28,820
It's strange, but if you want to laugh, it's okay to laugh.

398
00:22:28,820 --> 00:22:35,820
What I want to do is what I want to do.

399
00:22:35,820 --> 00:22:42,820
I want to see the same morning.

400
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:46,820
I want to choose the next day.

401
00:22:46,820 --> 00:22:51,820
I want to choose the next day.

402
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:54,820
I want to choose the next day.

403
00:23:16,820 --> 00:23:21,820
That's my crazy cyclone!

404
00:23:21,820 --> 00:23:22,820
Way cool, huh?

405
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:27,820
Actually, between you two, I'd say your head is the crazy cyclone.

406
00:23:27,820 --> 00:23:29,820
Who are you calling a cyclone?

407
00:23:29,820 --> 00:23:31,820
But the crazy part's fine.

408
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:39,820
We came for some boar hunting, but wound up facing much deadlier game.

409
00:23:39,820 --> 00:23:42,820
I won't let them get away with making everyone suffer!

410
00:23:42,820 --> 00:23:45,820
Black Clover, page nine.

411
00:23:45,820 --> 00:23:46,820
Beasts!

412
00:23:46,820 --> 00:23:48,820
My magic is never giving up!

